  "semantics": {
    "policy": "Active,modem,sleep banks retain their own writable fields. Sleep policies are not sleep transitions.",
    "clockApply": "Write-trigger immediate active func/APB updates require all-on banks; partial gating rejected atomically because it is not routed to every module. Active ICG selection only; source/sleep transition rejected.",
    "forceRelease": "Release of force-on/no-reset/no-isolate uses retained active policy. Asserted domain reset,isolation,powerdown or active CPU stall/hold remain Prohibited.",
    "ldo": "External LDO requested dref,mul,rail,ripple,current fields are stored; no analog voltage,waveform or calibration completion.",
    "biasConflict": "Fixed pmu_reg.h says LP/HP_DBIAS_VOL fields are RO default24; same pmu_ll.h writes13/28. Preserve header RO reset values and count attempted differences. DBIAS_INIT is a WT request counter,not calibrated voltage or done status.",
    "psram": "PMU_PSRAM_XPD bit31 reset0 is MPLL PHY enable per ldo_ll_enable(0). Actual bus PSRAM reads,writes and fetches require both PHY power and existing clock. No implicit RAM chip or map; backing bytes retained across PHY gating,not a power-loss retention model."
  },
